38 #edb/ref 17592186400002 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186105877 1038 #edb/ref 17592186399967 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186110577 1038 #edb/ref 17592186399925 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186110577 1038 #edb/ref 17592186399932 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186110593 1038 #edb/ref 17592186399960 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186110594 1038 #edb/ref 17592186399974 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186115187 1038 #edb/ref 17592186400009 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186115228 1038 #edb/ref 17592186400016 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186129088 1038 #edb/ref 17592186400162 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186129089 1038 #edb/ref 17592186400169 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186129224 1038 #edb/ref 17592186400036 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186129426 1068 #edb/ref 17592186126026 13194139533480 17592186045585 false] [17592186129426 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400030 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186129426 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186129426 1071 "Consider the expression $f(x, y) = 2x^{2}y$. What are the missing entries in the following sign table of $f(x, y)$?\n\n| $y > 0$ |  |  |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $y < 0$ |  |  |\n|  | $x < 0$ | $x > 0$ |" 13194139533480 17592186045585 false] [17592186129426 1071 "Consider the expression $f(x,y)=2{x}^{2}y.$ What are the missing entries in the following sign table of $f(x,y)?$\n\n| $y>0$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<0$ |  |  |\n|  | $x<0$ | $x>0$ |" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186129426 1074 "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=0$ and $y=0.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below.\n\n![](images/c3/c35c98904d2a0d0d6d49c582cd9f9dba9d96e91ae0da5deb2d329f38f77532e3.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](images/93/9340582eaad37c4ce1e0c8cbcdce48faec1e36c3c05adbedd61aa2de7168fd2f.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $2{x}^{2}$ | $y$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-Left | $(-1,1)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Top-Right | $(1,1)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(-1,-1)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(1,-1)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n\n \nUsing the *last* column of the table above, we get the following picture:\n\n![](images/7c/7c851189a040934728e1b312706b4727c141cc678a4be870b6057e281be6e0fd.png)\n\nFinally, we fill in the required sign table.\n\n| $y>0$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<0$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n|  | $x<0$ | $x>0$ |" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186166868 1038 #edb/ref 17592186400064 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186172095 1038 #edb/ref 17592186400113 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186175932 1038 #edb/ref 17592186400023 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186179707 1038 #edb/ref 17592186400043 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186179707 1038 #edb/ref 17592186400050 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186179707 1038 #edb/ref 17592186400057 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186198252 1038 #edb/ref 17592186399988 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399911 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399912 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399911 1069 "q-116564" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399911 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399911 1071 "Find the asymptotes of the hyperbola $8{y}^{2}-25{x}^{2}=200.$" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399911 1072 #uuid "8d94134c-ec88-57a5-9623-464fd1bd46e5" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399911 1074 "The standard equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}x.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the given equation in standard form, we divide both sides of the equation by $200$ and then simplify, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8{y}^{2}-25{x}^{2} & =200 \\\\ \\frac{8{y}^{2}}{200}-\\frac{25{x}^{2}}{200} & =\\frac{200}{200} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have $a=\\sqrt{25}=5,$ and $b=\\sqrt{8}=2\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are $y=\\pm \\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{2}}x=\\pm \\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{4}x.$" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399912 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399913 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399912 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399914 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399912 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399915 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399912 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399916 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399912 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399917 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399912 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399912 1077 "selection" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399912 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399915 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399912 1080 #uuid "6c38af93-79cc-5a2c-ab0d-50f123dc3b76" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399913 1081 "y=\\pm \\frac{5}{4}x" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399913 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399913 1084 #uuid "489d92c9-77a7-5316-943d-8961ddbc2299" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399914 1081 "y=\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}x" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399914 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399914 1084 #uuid "0783558f-bd5d-5ab2-b37e-b9fc4fecb054" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399915 1081 "y=\\pm \\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{4}x" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399915 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399915 1084 #uuid "3a6e08ec-dac3-5b7c-b5a5-af8e4b81a049" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399916 1081 "y=\\pm \\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{5}x" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399916 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399916 1084 #uuid "44d093ae-4ed6-57b8-a8f5-a1b5d3c397ba" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399917 1081 "y=\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}x" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399917 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399917 1084 #uuid "f60f0eb5-7238-5210-9677-0ea20e2d26bf" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399918 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399919 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399918 1069 "q-116618" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399918 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399918 1071 "Lisa is selling orange juice. The following table shows the rate, in liters per hour, at which it is sold.\n\n| $t\\,(\\text{hour})$ | $1$ | $2$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $c(t)\\,(\\text{lts/hour})$ | $3$ | $5$ | $7$ |\n\nUse the trapezoidal rule with the partition\n\n$$\n[1,2]\\cup [2,5],\n$$\n\nto approximate the total number of liters of juice sold by Lisa over a 4 hours period." 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399918 1072 #uuid "ff130200-2cc7-564b-a515-b5f1a6777878" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399918 1074 "In this context, we have $2$ trapezoids, and the area $A$ under the curve $y=c(t)$ represents the total number of liters sold over a $4$ period.\n\nUsing the trapezoidal rule, we estimate the area as follows:\n\n$$\nA≈\\frac{c(1)+c(2)}{2}\\cdot Δ{t}_{1}+\\frac{c(2)+c(5)}{2}\\cdot Δ{t}_{2}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the appropriate numbers into the above expression gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ≈\\frac{3+5}{2}\\cdot (2-1)+\\frac{5+7}{2}\\cdot (5-2) \\\\  & =4\\cdot 1+6\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =22\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Lisa sold approximately $22\\,\\text{liters}$ over a $4$ hours period." 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399919 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399920 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399919 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399921 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399919 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399922 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399919 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399923 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399919 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399924 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399919 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399919 1077 "selection" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399919 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399922 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399919 1080 #uuid "44600354-824b-592c-9161-175c33bd5952" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399920 1081 "$26$ liters" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399920 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399920 1084 #uuid "d5b366ab-ac37-5133-882b-090698ec969f" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399921 1081 "$18$ liters" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399921 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399921 1084 #uuid "8b91a9aa-9d15-594e-aad9-d38bd8e60406" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399922 1081 "$22$ liters" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399922 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399922 1084 #uuid "01b77170-2c7b-5940-82c2-eb220be7de45" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399923 1081 "$32$ liters" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399923 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399923 1084 #uuid "4059cbf3-390a-560a-9303-cb274ffe4e32" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399924 1081 "$11$ liters" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399924 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399924 1084 #uuid "d3ebefd3-a3c2-551f-b64f-510f1f0c1fb3" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399925 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399926 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399925 1069 "q-117010" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399925 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399925 1071 "Which of the following points lies on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x?$\n\nI. $(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\frac{2\\pi }{3})$\nII. $(0,0)$\nIII. $(-1,-\\frac{\\pi }{2})$" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399925 1072 #uuid "b17707f8-d0a8-5f70-818e-f01d27903349" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399925 1074 "In order for a point $(a,b)$ to lie on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x,$ the following conditions must hold:\n\n- The reflected point $(b,a)$ must lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ meaning $a=\\operatorname{sin}⁡b.$\n\n- The $y$-value of the point must lie in the range of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x,$ which is $y\\in [-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}].$\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of the points. \n\n- First, we consider the point $(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\frac{2\\pi }{3}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{2\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x$ is $y\\in [-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}],$ and $y=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$ does **not** lie within this range. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the point $(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\frac{2\\pi }{3})$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x.$\n\n- Next, we consider the point $(0,0).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(0,0)$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x$ is $y\\in [-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}],$ and $y=0$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(0,0)$ does lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x.$\n\n- Finally, we consider the point $(-1,-\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},-1)$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x$ is $y\\in [-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}],$ and $y=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(-1,-\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ does lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x.$" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399926 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399927 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399926 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399928 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399926 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399929 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399926 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399930 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399926 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399931 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399926 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399926 1077 "selection" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399926 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399928 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399926 1080 #uuid "6e322aae-9a1d-5f87-91ef-3c517a609bae" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399927 1081 "I, II, and III" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399927 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399927 1084 #uuid "c775d264-7add-50d0-9563-a7bc449e39af" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399928 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399928 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399928 1084 #uuid "b0c7aafc-ae2e-5787-820c-5402603bfece" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399929 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399929 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399929 1084 #uuid "2824858f-584d-5d06-a903-218ae60d0d62" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399930 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399930 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399930 1084 #uuid "e2713c21-9042-52eb-96d6-aa1c206f3f35" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399931 1081 "II only" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399931 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399931 1084 #uuid "0113c4eb-1180-5aef-8c3f-730b7f7828d6" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399932 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399933 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399932 1069 "q-117012" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399932 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399932 1071 "Which of the following points lies on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x?$\n\nI. $(\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})$\nII. $(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},-\\frac{\\pi }{3})$\nIII. $(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\frac{5\\pi }{4})$" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399932 1072 #uuid "8d72740e-6072-5046-bfdb-c5667ec877d5" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186399932 1074 "In order for a point $(a,b)$ to lie on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x,$ the following conditions must hold:\n\n- The reflected point $(b,a)$ must lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ meaning $a=\\operatorname{sin}⁡b.$\n\n- The $y$-value of the point must lie in the range of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x,$ which is $y\\in [-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}].$\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of the points. \n\n- First, we consider the point $(\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\frac{\\pi }{4})$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$  $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the point $(\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x.$\n\n- Next, we consider 