a057d8-e342-52dd-a1fb-abc1e06dc5c1" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400059 1081 "| $-$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $+$ | $+$ |" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400059 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400059 1084 #uuid "89a56145-d991-5f19-9125-7dfeb8c19018" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400060 1081 "| $-$ | $+$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $-$ | $+$ |" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400060 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400060 1084 #uuid "06d8b15d-ffbd-5909-a889-264a17e6ec09" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400061 1081 "| $+$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $-$ | $+$ |" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400061 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400061 1084 #uuid "ff298d2d-031a-50d5-a2e0-d484276129ef" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400062 1081 "| $+$ | $+$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $-$ | $-$ |" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400062 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400062 1084 #uuid "bc19913c-5667-515a-bb6f-f55140f312eb" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400063 1081 "| $+$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $+$ | $-$ |" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400063 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400063 1084 #uuid "af5764ad-7d4d-52f1-b5b0-d4fb0b6a16fc" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400064 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400065 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400064 1069 "q-122351" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400064 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400064 1071 "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis in the direction of increasing $x.$ When the displacement of $P$ from the origin $O$ is $x\\,\\text{m},$ its acceleration is $\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x+1}}\\,{m/s}^{2}.$ Initially, $P$ is at the origin $O$ and has velocity $v=4\\,m/s.$ Find $x$ as a function of time $t.$" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400064 1072 #uuid "528f1204-b150-5ae3-b3f2-1df94a35f90d" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400064 1074 "![](images/ee/ee516744d915553bf962b498af522cf0006d42c5d0e0e2a003e6f385dd069e4a.png)\n\nSince the acceleration of the particle $P$ is $\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x+1}}\\,{m/s}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x+1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2})\n$$\n\nwe can rewrite our equation as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2})=\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x+1}}.\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides of the above equation with respect to $x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x+1}}\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the general solution\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2} & =8\\sqrt{x+1}+K.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $x=0\\,\\text{m}$ when $v=4\\,\\text{m/s},$ we can find the value of the constant $K,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2} & =8\\sqrt{x+1}+K \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}(4)^{2} & =8\\sqrt{0+1}+K \\\\ 8 & =8+K \\\\ K & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2} & =8\\sqrt{x+1} \\\\ {v}^{2} & =16\\sqrt{x+1} \\\\ v & =\\pm 4\\sqrt[4]{x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the particle is moving in the direction of increasing  $x,$ we have that $v(x)>0,$ so we can discard the negative square root. Therefore,\n\n$$\nv(x)=4\\sqrt[4]{x+1}.\n$$\n\nNow, we know that $v=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}.$ Therefore, we have the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=4\\sqrt[4]{x+1}.\n$$\n\nSeparating the variables and integrating both sides with respect to $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =4\\sqrt[4]{x+1} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt[4]{x+1}}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =4 \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt[4]{x+1}}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int 4\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\frac{4}{3}(x+1)^{3/4} & =4t+{C}_{1} \\\\ (x+1)^{3/4} & =3t+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=\\frac{3{C}_{1}}{4}.$ \n\nWe're given that $x=0$ when $t=0.$ Therefore, $C=1,$ and the particular solution is\n\n$$\n(x+1)^{3/4}=3t+1.\n$$\n\nFinally, writing $x$ in terms of $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+1)^{3/4} & =3t+1 \\\\ x+1 & =(3t+1)^{4/3} \\\\ x & =(3t+1)^{4/3}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400065 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400066 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400065 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400067 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400065 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400068 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400065 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400069 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400065 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400070 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400065 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400065 1077 "selection" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400065 1079 #edb/ref 17592186400067 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400065 1080 #uuid "56af02a6-0883-5dcb-9c23-0114fa511fa6" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400066 1081 "x(t)=(3t+1)^{4}-1" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400066 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400066 1084 #uuid "cb841386-1180-59be-8b8f-ef4a3bdf4bae" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400067 1081 "x(t)=(3t+1)^{4/3}-1" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400067 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400067 1084 #uuid "e0471f0f-25c1-5626-b98b-3b2fe326dc7c" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400068 1081 "x(t)=(4t+1)^{3}-1" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400068 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400068 1084 #uuid "6e