ies is divergent  because $|r|\\ge 1.$\n\nIn conclusion, only series II converges." 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400156 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400157 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400156 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400158 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400156 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400159 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400156 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400160 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400156 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400161 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400156 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400156 1077 "selection" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400156 1079 #edb/ref 17592186400161 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400156 1080 #uuid "7478616a-dd06-5aea-b75a-b73c688ab5fc" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400157 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400157 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400157 1084 #uuid "e3c60d79-86b9-50cc-9f64-560ea2cecec3" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400158 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400158 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400158 1084 #uuid "04fc169e-d7b2-5fb6-aaaa-03529f82ef7a" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400159 1081 "I only" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400159 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400159 1084 #uuid "c64b1ae1-73f4-50e4-83d1-af39cac88db8" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400160 1081 "III only" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400160 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400160 1084 #uuid "c0007124-207e-55b6-82bb-cf42de7dce86" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400161 1081 "II only" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400161 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400161 1084 #uuid "8d3720ee-33a3-5bc3-abd0-5c477d7133fe" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400162 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400163 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400162 1069 "q-124965" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400162 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400162 1071 "![](images/cd/cd41c969aee2e7c04c9034106978d8522d6a715733098bfde87abbdb861da7a8.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the unit circle. Given that $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{4},$ what is the value of $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta ?$" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400162 1072 #uuid "6bb1887b-828c-58c3-9b10-3c0e7dc6d40b" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400162 1074 "![](images/49/4942cec8983dd2bddddd0ba2f8f9332b1b82f3999a44adb138b905457d39c633.png)\n\nWe can use the Pythagorean identity to find $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1 \\\\ {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{4}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-\\frac{1}{16}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{15}{16}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe select the negative answer since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ is negative in the second quadrant. So, $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =-\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{4}.$\n\nFinally, knowing that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{4})}{(-\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{4})}=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{15}}=-\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{15}.\n$$" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400163 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400164 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400163 1075 #