e] [17592186400168 1084 #uuid "df3a9c05-b642-53bc-aee7-47f4b93b0bb0" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400169 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400170 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400169 1069 "q-125004" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400169 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400169 1071 "If $sin⁡\\theta =\\frac{7}{8}$ and $\\frac{\\pi }{2}<\\theta <\\pi $ then what is the value of $sec⁡\\theta ?$" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400169 1072 #uuid "c006e542-29a2-5102-8308-98f4920ebd17" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400169 1074 "Let's sketch our angle $\\theta $ in the coordinate plane.\n\n![](images/5c/5c98414bbe0e1e373864e9ec1d6b8667bb0032c8824f20bed1e6f9b9079c4d02.png)\n\nWe're given that $sin⁡\\theta =\\frac{7}{8}.$ We can use the Pythagorean identity to find $cos⁡\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1 \\\\ {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ cos⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $sin⁡\\theta =\\frac{7}{8}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cos⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{(\\frac{7}{8})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-\\frac{49}{64}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{15}{64}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe select the negative answer since $cos⁡\\theta $ is negative in the second quadrant. So, $cos⁡\\theta =-\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{8}.$\n\nFinally, knowing that $sec⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{cos⁡\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\nsec⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{(-\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{8})}=-\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{15}}=-\\frac{8\\sqrt{15}}{15}.\n$$" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400170 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400171 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400170 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400172 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400170 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400173 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400170 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400174 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400170 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400175 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400170 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400170 1077 "selection" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400170 1079 #edb/ref 17592186400173 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400170 1080 #uuid "77272688-3fb6-5eaf-8b2d-59ba189820e4" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400171 1081 "sec⁡\\theta =8\\sqrt{15}" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400171 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400171 1084 #uuid "cbeb0313-5651-561b-a4b7-42ac4f88f1ff" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400172 1081 "sec⁡\\theta =\\frac{8\\sqrt{15}}{15}" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400172 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400172 1084 #uuid "1a165698-e8f8-506c-9756-3955aee8c79d" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400173 1081 "sec⁡\\theta =-\\frac{8\\sqrt{15}}{15}" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400173 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400173 1084 #uuid "32a56d6b-1f3c-53ed-9db5-88987f60fdbc" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400174 1081 "sec⁡\\theta =-\\frac{4\\sqrt{15}}{3}" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400174 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400174 1084 #uuid "9c3e631f-f822-5565-8077-5a496dd0604b" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400175 1081 "sec⁡\\theta =-8\\sqrt{15}" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400175 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400175 1084 #uuid "0944c75f-3871-5029-b2ac-06fe51638caa" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400176 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400177 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400176 1069 "q-125262" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400176 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400176 1071 "Which of the following functions satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem over the interval $[0,e]?$\n\nI. $f(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}$\nII. $g(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$\nIII. $h(x)={e}^{-x/2}$" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400176 1072 #uuid "0d26c1fd-9972-5992-b3ee-1cc9fed13d91" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400176 1074 "For a function to satisfy the conditions of the mean value theorem over the interval $[0,e],$ the function must be continuous on $[0,e]$ and differentiable on $(0,e).$\n\nLet's check each function individually.\n\n- The function $f(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}$ is continuous and differentiable on $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ In particular, it  is continuous on $[0,e]$ and differentiable on $(0,e).$ Therefore, $f(x)$ satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function  $g(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ is not defined at $x=0,$ so it is not continuous at $x=0,$ which means it is not continuous on $[0,e].$ Therefore, $g(x)$ does not satisfy the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function $h(x)={e}^{-x/2}$ is continuous and differentiable on $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ In particular, it  is continuous on $[0,e]$ and differentiable on $(0,e).$ Therefore, $h(x)$ satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\nTherefore, only functions I and III satisfy the conditions for the mean value theorem over the interval $[0,e].$" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400177 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400178 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400177 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400179 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400177 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400180 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400177 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400181 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400177 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400182 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400177 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400177 1077 "selection" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400177 1079 #edb/ref 17592186400180 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400177 1080 #uuid "2ce3352c-5866-54ec-8397-cf9e37019fd3" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400178 1081 "I, II, and III" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400178 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400178 1084 #uuid "95363d69-aef8-5be0-bed6-2e48e831157e" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400179 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400179 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400179 1084 #uuid "c811cfee-b520-5024-a08a-7253a95a06d9" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400180 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400180 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400180 1084 #uuid "fb4caf99-22b3-54c0-8115-85030a8148f5" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400181 1081 "III only" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400181 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400181 1084 #uuid "7f361f8f-c150-58fe-9b01-71b7b26b992c" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400182 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400182 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400182 1084 #uuid "f957daf2-0051-5201-9483-2ef71d3af41d" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400183 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400184 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400183 1069 "q-125335" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400183 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400183 1071 "Express the Maclaurin series expansion for $x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ given by\n\n$$\nx\\operatorname{sin}⁡x={x}^{2}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{3!}+\\frac{{x}^{6}}{5!}-\\frac{{x}^{8}}{7!}+⋯\n$$\n\nusing sigma notation." 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400183 1072 #uuid "66708e85-e31b-5700-a1e3-46ef23b1df08" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400183 1074 "The first four terms of the series are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & ={x}^{2} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{3!} \\\\ {a}_{2} & =\\frac{{x}^{6}}{5!} \\\\ {a}_{3} & =-\\frac{{x}^{8}}{7!}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we can express these terms using a common format, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{(-1)^{0}{x}^{2\\cdot (0+1)}}{(2\\cdot 0+1)!} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =\\frac{(-1)^{1}{x}^{2\\cdot (1+1)}}{(2\\cdot 1+1)!} \\\\ {a}_{2} & =\\frac{(-1)^{2}{x}^{2\\cdot (2+1)}}{(2\\cdot 2+1)!} \\\\ {a}_{3} & =\\frac{(-1)^{3}{x}^{2\\cdot (3+1)}}{(2\\cdot 3+1)!}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe deduce that the general formula for the $n$th term is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{(-1)^{n}{x}^{2(n+1)}}{(2n+1)!}\\,.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & ={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n}{x}^{2(n+1)}}{(2n+1)!}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400184 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400185 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400184 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400186 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400184 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400187 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400184 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400188 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400184 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400189 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400184 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400184 1077 "selection" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400184 1079 #edb/ref 17592186400186 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400184 1080 #uuid "5d66455f-0c62-5cd9-9133-6e646aa1100a" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400185 1081 "x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}{x}^{n+2}}{(n+1)!}" 13194139533480 17592186045585 true] [17592186400185 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533480 17592186045585 true]